            $TRANS$As the dictionary grows, it is necessary to create a new table that re-hashes. Not good in terms of tolerant retrieval. • The structure of a timber is an abstract model of a hierarchical structure. It consists of a collection of nodes (vertices) with a father-son ratio. Each vertex has a maximum of two sons. Complexity (n) O(log) Saving a dictionary using a binary search tree – we will build the tree and each time we go down a level we will divide by half. Summary: - Search time O(logM) – where M is the length of the list. - When the dictionary grows it is necessary to balance the list which can take time.$TRANS$
