            $TRANS$In 20 documents, they agreed that they were relevant out of the 50. In 15 documents, they agreed that they were irrelevant out of the 50. In other words, the two of them agreed together on 35 documents that are relevant and irrelevant. The disagreements between them are for 15 documents (5 documents plus 10 documents). P(A) – Probability of agreement = (20 + 15)/50 = 0.7 P(E) – The probability that the judges agreed due to luck. The first judge said yes 30 times (30/50=60%), the second judge said yes 25 times (50%), it is possible that there is a mistake here, if this is a case where the judge has a tendency to say yes.$TRANS$
