            $TRANS$Shingling a set of k consecutive characters in our example K=5 In our example there are 2 documents - "The cat sat on the chair" and "The cat sat on the sofa" We will create sequences from them according to the k given to us. For example: the c, he ca, e cat, and so on. In mathematics, a set is an unsorted collection of elements that differ from one another. The group allows you to add, remove, and find an element. If we add an existing element, the operation will not be performed. If we try to remove an element that does not exist, the action will not be performed. In the documents we will work on the groups that are without duplicates.$TRANS$
