            $TRANS$A sparse matrix is inefficient because the search is inefficient and there is a waste of space (0 does not constitute information and therefore since most zeros waste a lot of space). The information will take up a lot of space, let's say there are a million documents, when a document can be an entire book or just a chapter from it, an email, etc. Let's say that each document has 1000 words and each word takes up 6 bytes. The memory that will be required is 6 GB- x6 3 x10 6 10 We want to optimize the storage of the indexes. Inverted Index An inverted index is an index that maps from terms to documents. The documents are kept sorted according to predetermined numbering.$TRANS$
