            470,
            89,
            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "5d7fd2ac-3f2b-4775-9aa6-37305d00178a", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.279Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: טווחים, עץ, גבולות, קבוצה, אות"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.279000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Scopes • Every time you descend the tree, a signal is added to each of the boundaries of the ranges. For example, we came out of the A-M range. We divided into two groups: - First group A-F. Add another letter z to the upper limit and we get the limit a-fz. - Second group g-m. An additional letter A is added to the lower limit and we get the ga-m boundary. • We will go down another level, and we will divide the group A-FZ into two groups: - The first group: A-C. Add two more letters z to the upper limit and we get the limit a- czz. - Second group: d-fz. Two more letters A are added to the lower limit and we get the border daa- fz.$TRANS$
