            $TRANS$In order to distinguish between search engine idealism, we will use the following measures: • Precision – consists of a fraction that contains in the denominator all the images returned in the search engine (how many images were returned) and in the numerator what is relevant to the search we performed in the query (how many dogs did I get), i.e. 8 images were returned, of which 5 were of dogs (5/8).  • Recall – consists of a fraction that contains in the denominator everything that is relevant in the entire database (i.e., all the pictures of the dogs in the database), and in the counter what is relevant from what has been returned, i.e. the database consists of 12 images, of which 5 are relevant in the retrieved search (5/12).    ?$TRANS$
