            $TRANS$It is possible that one carrier will have a greater number of documents than another carrier. Groups are supposed to be formed, each containing documents. Now we will enter the query, compare it against all the carriers () and then compare it with the documents in the same carrier group to know which document is closest to it, that is, in our example for 100 documents we will compare against a total of 20 documents (against the top 10 and against the remaining 9 documents in the carrier group), so that we have narrowed down the comparisons we could make - instead of checking N documents, we will check.$TRANS$
