            $TRANS$When the term in the query does not appear in the dictionary, the denominator is equal to zero and we get zero by division. The formula can be updated as follows: In our reading book there is no reference to the formula, so you can decide that if this is the case, we will write =0 t idf. In our case there are 6 documents (N) and the word Brurus appears 3 times so we will get the score of 0.33, on the other hand the word Mercy is very common so its score will be lower and we can see it - you will get the score of 0.08. Let's connect the two requirements – IDF weighting-tf, a concept that appears more frequently, provides more information, allows a concept that appears less frequently.$TRANS$
