            $TRANS$RP PR F + 2 In the following example: we will use K-precision (and determine that we want a sample of 6 documents) we will look at the first 6 documents and at this point we will consider precision and recall. Number of relevant results = 5. Precision- 4/6=0.67 Recall- 4/5=0.8 73.0 47.1 072.1 8.067.0 8.0*67.0*22 == + = + = RP PR F How we arrived at the composite index we averaged the inverse value of the two indices. We reversed the index, what we calculated was the harmonious average. A harmonic mean is a type of mean, that is, it is the inverse of the arithmetic average of the inverses.$TRANS$
