            $TRANS$True or False Example: No steaming: Mouse → 1 mouse → 2 doves → 3 pigeons → 4 dog → 5 dogs → 6 with steaming: mouse → 1 → 2 doves → 3 → 4 → 6 dog → 5 → 6 • In a Boolean retrieval system, steaming never lowers precision. Q. False, when steaming the number of documents will increase, i.e. in precision the denominator increases, so even if we don't know the change in the counter, the denominator necessarily reduces the fraction. For example, without steaming, we want to return a mouse, let's say a mouse returned and a pigeon, so the precision will be 1/2.$TRANS$
