            $TRANS$Between the two documents we can see that there are 13 sequences that are identical. Calculate the Jaccard index: 13 refers to the groups that are identical in the two documents 21 refers to all the groups shown in the two documents that are not identical (in the first document the c appears twice, so we will count once). In another example, we will create sequences for the statement A rose is a rose is a rose. At the level of words, where k=4: a rose is a rose is a rose is a rose, the next sequence creates a duplication, identical to the first sequence. We will create a signature for each sequence, we will produce a 64-bit signature for each sequence so that we have a large space of possibilities.$TRANS$
